IMPORT prelude
IMPORT types

-- Online Safety (Minimum Age and Child Safety Risk Assessment) Bill (NZ)
-- Part 2 -- Duties on operators of age-restricted platforms (cll 11 to 19).
-- Source: registers/source-bundle/LMS1592864.xml, 2026 No 339-1, retrieved 2026-09-11.
--
-- Every duty in this Part attaches to "an operator of an age-restricted
-- platform". Whether a person is that operator is decided in
-- part-1-preliminary.l4 (cll 5 to 8); this module assumes it and asks what is
-- owed. Deadlines follow the WA Residential Tenancies Act convention: WITHIN
-- takes a number of days. See the interpretation note on `days in 12 months`.

§ `Part 2 -- Duties on operators of age-restricted platforms`

§§ `Actors and actions`

DECLARE `duty actor` IS ONE OF
    `the operator`
    `the regulator`

DECLARE `duty action` IS ONE OF
    `take reasonable steps to prevent a New Zealand person under 16 from having an account`
    `stop keeping personal information collected for the age assurance purpose`
    `undertake a child safety risk assessment`
    `provide the child safety risk assessment to the regulator`
    `review the child safety risk assessment`
    `provide the reviewed child safety risk assessment to the regulator`
    `undertake a change-related child safety risk assessment before making the change`
    `provide the change-related child safety risk assessment to the regulator`
    `designate an individual responsible for confirming the accuracy of risk assessments`
    `provide the repeated risk assessment to the regulator`
    `notify the Privacy Commissioner before applying for a court-imposed remedy`

§§ `Interpretation of periods`

-- INTERPRETATION CALL, flagged for the reviewer. cll 15, 16 and Schedule 1 all
-- express periods in months, and WITHIN takes days. 365 is used for a 12-month
-- period and 183 for 6 months. Nothing in the Bill turns on the difference at
-- present, but any rule that compares two such periods would inherit the
-- rounding, so this constant is named rather than inlined.

`days in 12 months` MEANS 365
`days in 6 months`  MEANS 183

§§ `11. Operators must take steps to prevent persons under 16 years from having accounts`

DECLARE `age assurance` HAS
    name                                                                                IS A STRING
    -- cl 11(1)
    `takes steps to prevent a New Zealand person under 16 from having an account`        IS A BOOLEAN
    -- cl 11(2): manual entry of age or date of birth is not a reasonable step
    `the only step taken is requiring manual entry of age or date of birth`              IS A BOOLEAN
    -- cl 11(3)(a), (b) and (c)
    `the only step taken is requiring an approved evidence of age document`              IS A BOOLEAN
    `the only step taken is using a digital identity service`                            IS A BOOLEAN
    `the only steps taken are an evidence of age document and a digital identity service` IS A BOOLEAN
    -- the residue of "reasonable steps", left as an evaluative standard
    `the steps taken are otherwise reasonable`                                           IS A BOOLEAN
    -- cl 11(4)
    `collects personal information of a class that regulations under section 63 forbid`  IS A BOOLEAN

-- cll 11(2) and 11(3) say only what does NOT discharge the duty. Each limb is a
-- disqualifier: a step of that kind, taken alone, cannot satisfy cl 11(1).

GIVEN a IS A `age assurance`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the steps taken cannot satisfy the duty` IF
        a's `the only step taken is requiring manual entry of age or date of birth`
    OR  a's `the only step taken is requiring an approved evidence of age document`
    OR  a's `the only step taken is using a digital identity service`
    OR  a's `the only steps taken are an evidence of age document and a digital identity service`

-- What remains once the disqualifiers are removed is "reasonable steps", which
-- the Bill does not define -- see NOTES.md, probe 5. The encoding keeps that
-- residue visible as its own field rather than folding it into the disqualifiers.

@ref Online Safety (Minimum Age and Child Safety Risk Assessment) Bill (NZ) cl 11
@export Decide whether an operator satisfies the minimum age duty in clause 11(1)
GIVEN a IS A `age assurance` @desc What the operator does to keep under-16s off the platform: whether it takes steps at all, whether the only step is manual age entry, an evidence of age document, a digital identity service or the last two together, and whether what it does is otherwise reasonable.
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the operator satisfies the duty in section 11(1)` IF
        a's `takes steps to prevent a New Zealand person under 16 from having an account`
    AND NOT `the steps taken cannot satisfy the duty` a
    AND a's `the steps taken are otherwise reasonable`

-- cl 11(4): a separate prohibition, not a condition of the cl 11(1) duty.
GIVEN a IS A `age assurance`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the operator contravenes section 11(4)` IF
    a's `collects personal information of a class that regulations under section 63 forbid`

GIVEN a IS A `age assurance`
GIVETH A DEONTIC `duty actor` `duty action`
DECIDE `the minimum age duty` IS
    IF `the operator satisfies the duty in section 11(1)` a
    THEN FULFILLED
    ELSE
        PARTY `the operator`
        MUST `take reasonable steps to prevent a New Zealand person under 16 from having an account`
        WITHIN 0
        HENCE FULFILLED
        LEST BREACH BY `the operator` BECAUSE "reasonable steps were not taken to prevent a New Zealand person under 16 years from having an account (cl 11(1))"

§§ `12. Personal information collected for the purpose of complying with duty, 13. Breach`

DECLARE `personal information handling` HAS
    name                                                                                IS A STRING
    -- cl 12(1)(a)
    `keeps the information for longer than the age assurance purpose requires`           IS A BOOLEAN
    -- cl 12(1)(b)
    `uses or discloses the information for a purpose other than the age assurance purpose` IS A BOOLEAN
    -- cl 13(1)
    `the conduct was that of a person holding the information for or on behalf of the operator` IS A BOOLEAN
    -- cl 13(3)
    `the regulator notified the Privacy Commissioner before applying to the High Court`  IS A BOOLEAN

GIVEN h IS A `personal information handling`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `section 12(1)(a) is contravened` IF
    h's `keeps the information for longer than the age assurance purpose requires`

GIVEN h IS A `personal information handling`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `section 12(1)(b) is contravened` IF
    h's `uses or discloses the information for a purpose other than the age assurance purpose`

-- cl 13(1): a contravention by a person who holds the information for or on
-- behalf of the operator is treated as a contravention BY the operator. The
-- operator is therefore liable on either route, which is why the holder fact is
-- not a condition of the rule below.

@ref Online Safety (Minimum Age and Child Safety Risk Assessment) Bill (NZ) cll 12, 13(1)
@export Decide whether an operator contravenes the personal information restrictions in clause 12(1)
GIVEN h IS A `personal information handling` @desc How the personal information collected for age assurance was handled: whether it was kept longer than that purpose required, whether it was used or disclosed for any other purpose, and whether the conduct was that of a person holding it on the operator's behalf.
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the operator contravenes section 12(1)` IF
        `section 12(1)(a) is contravened` h
    OR  `section 12(1)(b) is contravened` h

-- cl 13(2): such a contravention is treated as an interference with the privacy
-- of an individual for the purposes of Parts 5 and 6 of the Privacy Act 2020.
GIVEN h IS A `personal information handling`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the contravention is an interference with privacy under the Privacy Act 2020` IF
    `the operator contravenes section 12(1)` h

-- cl 13(3): a duty on the REGULATOR, not the operator.
GIVEN h IS A `personal information handling`
GIVETH A DEONTIC `duty actor` `duty action`
DECIDE `the duty to notify the Privacy Commissioner` IS
    IF h's `the regulator notified the Privacy Commissioner before applying to the High Court`
    THEN FULFILLED
    ELSE
        PARTY `the regulator`
        MUST `notify the Privacy Commissioner before applying for a court-imposed remedy`
        WITHIN 0
        HENCE FULFILLED
        LEST BREACH BY `the regulator` BECAUSE "the Privacy Commissioner was not notified before the regulator applied to the High Court for a court-imposed remedy in respect of a contravention of cl 12(1) (cl 13(3))"

§§ `14. Operators must undertake child safety risk assessment`

-- cl 14(2) lists the matters to be assessed; cl 14(3) lists what the written
-- assessment must include. The content of each limb is evaluative ("the level of
-- risk"), so each is modelled as a single fact about adequacy rather than
-- decomposed. cl 19 turns on exactly these adequacy judgements.

DECLARE `child safety risk assessment` HAS
    name                                                                                IS A STRING
    `has been undertaken`                                                               IS A BOOLEAN
    `is in writing`                                                                     IS A BOOLEAN
    -- cl 14(2)(a) to (d): the matters assessed
    `adequately assesses the risk of children encountering the content in section 14(2)(a)` IS A BOOLEAN
    `adequately assesses the design, features, functionality and operation risk`         IS A BOOLEAN
    `adequately assesses the advertising risk`                                           IS A BOOLEAN
    `adequately assesses any matter specified by the regulator under section 14(2)(d)`    IS A BOOLEAN
    -- cl 14(3)(a) to (d): what the assessment must include
    `states the number of children who use the platform, broken down by age`             IS A BOOLEAN
    `describes the identified levels of risk and the reasons for them`                   IS A BOOLEAN
    `describes the measures in place, their efficacy and how efficacy is monitored`      IS A BOOLEAN
    `describes the assessment method and the method of review under section 16`          IS A BOOLEAN

GIVEN r IS A `child safety risk assessment`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the assessment covers every matter in section 14(2)` IF
        r's `adequately assesses the risk of children encountering the content in section 14(2)(a)`
    AND r's `adequately assesses the design, features, functionality and operation risk`
    AND r's `adequately assesses the advertising risk`
    AND r's `adequately assesses any matter specified by the regulator under section 14(2)(d)`

GIVEN r IS A `child safety risk assessment`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the assessment includes every matter in section 14(3)` IF
        r's `is in writing`
    AND r's `states the number of children who use the platform, broken down by age`
    AND r's `describes the identified levels of risk and the reasons for them`
    AND r's `describes the measures in place, their efficacy and how efficacy is monitored`
    AND r's `describes the assessment method and the method of review under section 16`

@ref Online Safety (Minimum Age and Child Safety Risk Assessment) Bill (NZ) cl 14
@export Decide whether a child safety risk assessment complies with clause 14
GIVEN r IS A `child safety risk assessment` @desc The assessment: whether it has been undertaken and is in writing, whether it adequately assesses each of the four matters in cl 14(2), and whether it includes each of the four things cl 14(3) requires.
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the child safety risk assessment complies with section 14` IF
        r's `has been undertaken`
    AND `the assessment covers every matter in section 14(2)` r
    AND `the assessment includes every matter in section 14(3)` r

§§ `15. Provision of child safety risk assessment to regulator, 16. Review`

DECLARE `assessment cycle` HAS
    name                                                                                IS A STRING
    -- cl 15(1)(b) and 16(3): the regulator may bring a date forward
    `the regulator has specified an earlier date by written notice`                      IS A BOOLEAN
    `the regulator is satisfied that an earlier date is desirable because of potential risk` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the regulator is satisfied that an earlier date is practicable for the operator`     IS A BOOLEAN
    -- performance
    `the assessment was provided to the regulator by the required date`                   IS A BOOLEAN
    `the review was completed within the required period`                                 IS A BOOLEAN
    `a copy was provided to the regulator on completion of the review`                    IS A BOOLEAN

-- cll 15(2) and 16(3) impose the same two-limb gate on bringing a date forward.
@ref Online Safety (Minimum Age and Child Safety Risk Assessment) Bill (NZ) cll 15(2), 16(3)
GIVEN c IS A `assessment cycle`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the regulator may specify an earlier date` IF
        c's `the regulator is satisfied that an earlier date is desirable because of potential risk`
    AND c's `the regulator is satisfied that an earlier date is practicable for the operator`

-- cl 15(1)(a): the default is 12 months after the date on which the platform
-- meets the definition of age-restricted platform.
@ref Online Safety (Minimum Age and Child Safety Risk Assessment) Bill (NZ) cl 15
GIVEN c IS A `assessment cycle`
GIVETH A DEONTIC `duty actor` `duty action`
DECIDE `the duty to provide the first assessment` IS
    IF c's `the assessment was provided to the regulator by the required date`
    THEN FULFILLED
    ELSE
        PARTY `the operator`
        MUST `provide the child safety risk assessment to the regulator`
        WITHIN `days in 12 months`
        HENCE FULFILLED
        LEST BREACH BY `the operator` BECAUSE "a copy of the child safety risk assessment was not provided to the regulator within 12 months after the platform met the definition of age-restricted platform, or by any earlier date specified by the regulator (cl 15(1))"

-- cl 16(2): a review must be completed within 12 months after the assessment was
-- completed, and within every 12-month period after the last review.
@ref Online Safety (Minimum Age and Child Safety Risk Assessment) Bill (NZ) cl 16
GIVEN c IS A `assessment cycle`
GIVETH A DEONTIC `duty actor` `duty action`
DECIDE `the duty to review the assessment` IS
    IF c's `the review was completed within the required period`
    THEN FULFILLED
    ELSE
        PARTY `the operator`
        MUST `review the child safety risk assessment`
        WITHIN `days in 12 months`
        HENCE FULFILLED
        LEST BREACH BY `the operator` BECAUSE "the child safety risk assessment was not reviewed within the 12-month period required by cl 16(2), or by any earlier date specified by the regulator under cl 16(3)"

-- cl 16(5): a copy must be provided on completion of a review, whether or not
-- the review changed anything.
GIVEN c IS A `assessment cycle`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the operator complies with section 16(5)` IF
    c's `a copy was provided to the regulator on completion of the review`

§§ `17. Change-related child safety risk assessments`

DECLARE `change related assessment` HAS
    name                                                                                IS A STRING
    -- cl 17(4): significant change includes design, features or functionality, or terms of use
    `the proposed change is a significant change to design, features or functionality`   IS A BOOLEAN
    `the proposed change is a significant change to the terms of use`                    IS A BOOLEAN
    -- cl 17(1) and (2)
    `an assessment of the section 14(2) matters was undertaken before the change was made` IS A BOOLEAN
    `is in writing`                                                                     IS A BOOLEAN
    `describes the anticipated levels of risk and the reasons for them`                  IS A BOOLEAN
    `describes current measures, their expected efficacy and any additional measures`    IS A BOOLEAN
    `describes the method used to assess the section 14(2) matters for the change`       IS A BOOLEAN
    -- cl 17(3)
    `a copy was provided to the regulator as soon as practicable after the assessment`   IS A BOOLEAN
    `a copy was provided to the regulator before the change was made`                    IS A BOOLEAN

-- cl 17(4) is inclusive ("includes"), so the two named limbs do not exhaust
-- significant change. The encoding follows the text: these are sufficient, not
-- necessary. A change outside both limbs may still be significant.
GIVEN c IS A `change related assessment`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the proposed change is a significant change` IF
        c's `the proposed change is a significant change to design, features or functionality`
    OR  c's `the proposed change is a significant change to the terms of use`

GIVEN c IS A `change related assessment`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the change-related assessment includes every matter in section 17(2)` IF
        c's `is in writing`
    AND c's `describes the anticipated levels of risk and the reasons for them`
    AND c's `describes current measures, their expected efficacy and any additional measures`
    AND c's `describes the method used to assess the section 14(2) matters for the change`

@ref Online Safety (Minimum Age and Child Safety Risk Assessment) Bill (NZ) cl 17
@export Decide whether an operator complies with clause 17 in relation to a proposed significant change
GIVEN c IS A `change related assessment` @desc The proposed change and the assessment made for it: whether the change is significant, whether an assessment of the cl 14(2) matters was undertaken before the change was made, what the assessment describes, and when a copy reached the regulator.
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the operator complies with section 17` IF
    IF   `the proposed change is a significant change` c
    THEN     c's `an assessment of the section 14(2) matters was undertaken before the change was made`
         AND `the change-related assessment includes every matter in section 17(2)` c
         AND c's `a copy was provided to the regulator as soon as practicable after the assessment`
         AND c's `a copy was provided to the regulator before the change was made`
    ELSE TRUE

§§ `18. Individual responsible for confirming accuracy of risk assessments`

DECLARE `responsible individual designation` HAS
    name                                                                                IS A STRING
    `an individual has been designated by notice to the regulator`                       IS A BOOLEAN
    -- cl 18(2)
    `the individual has a significant role in ensuring or overseeing the risk assessments` IS A BOOLEAN
    -- cl 18(3)
    `the notice specifies the designated individual's contact details`                   IS A BOOLEAN

@ref Online Safety (Minimum Age and Child Safety Risk Assessment) Bill (NZ) cl 18
@export Decide whether an operator has validly designated the individual responsible for confirming the accuracy of its risk assessments
GIVEN d IS A `responsible individual designation` @desc The designation: whether an individual has been designated by notice to the regulator, whether that individual has a significant role in ensuring or overseeing the operator's risk assessments, and whether the notice gives their contact details.
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the operator has validly designated a responsible individual` IF
        d's `an individual has been designated by notice to the regulator`
    AND d's `the individual has a significant role in ensuring or overseeing the risk assessments`
    AND d's `the notice specifies the designated individual's contact details`

§§ `19. Regulator's power to direct operator to repeat risk assessment`

DECLARE `repeat direction` HAS
    name                                                                                IS A STRING
    `the direction relates to a change-related child safety risk assessment`             IS A BOOLEAN
    -- cl 19(2)(a)
    `the regulator considers a section 14(2) matter was not adequately assessed`         IS A BOOLEAN
    `the regulator considers a section 14(3) matter is not adequately specified or described` IS A BOOLEAN
    -- cl 19(2)(b)
    `the regulator considers a section 14(2) matter was not adequately assessed for the change` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the regulator considers a section 17(2) matter is not adequately described`          IS A BOOLEAN
    -- cl 19(3)
    `the notice specifies the matters not adequately assessed, specified or described`    IS A BOOLEAN
    `the notice specifies the date by which the repeated assessment must be provided`     IS A BOOLEAN
    `the repeated assessment was provided by the date specified`                          IS A BOOLEAN

GIVEN d IS A `repeat direction`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a ground for directing a repeat exists` IF
    IF   d's `the direction relates to a change-related child safety risk assessment`
    THEN     d's `the regulator considers a section 14(2) matter was not adequately assessed for the change`
          OR d's `the regulator considers a section 17(2) matter is not adequately described`
    ELSE     d's `the regulator considers a section 14(2) matter was not adequately assessed`
          OR d's `the regulator considers a section 14(3) matter is not adequately specified or described`

@ref Online Safety (Minimum Age and Child Safety Risk Assessment) Bill (NZ) cl 19
@export Decide whether the regulator may direct an operator to repeat a risk assessment
GIVEN d IS A `repeat direction` @desc The direction: whether it concerns a change-related assessment, which inadequacy the regulator considers to exist, and what the written notice specifies.
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the regulator may direct the operator to repeat the assessment` IF
        `a ground for directing a repeat exists` d
    AND d's `the notice specifies the matters not adequately assessed, specified or described`
    AND d's `the notice specifies the date by which the repeated assessment must be provided`

§§ `Scenario fixtures`

-- An operator doing real age assurance beyond the disqualified methods.
`compliant age assurance` MEANS `age assurance` WITH
    name                                                                                 IS "facial estimation plus behavioural signals"
    `takes steps to prevent a New Zealand person under 16 from having an account`         IS TRUE
    `the only step taken is requiring manual entry of age or date of birth`               IS FALSE
    `the only step taken is requiring an approved evidence of age document`               IS FALSE
    `the only step taken is using a digital identity service`                             IS FALSE
    `the only steps taken are an evidence of age document and a digital identity service` IS FALSE
    `the steps taken are otherwise reasonable`                                            IS TRUE
    `collects personal information of a class that regulations under section 63 forbid`   IS FALSE

-- The cl 11(3)(c) case: both of the formal identity routes, and nothing else.
`identity documents only` MEANS `age assurance` WITH
    name                                                                                 IS "evidence of age document plus digital identity service"
    `takes steps to prevent a New Zealand person under 16 from having an account`         IS TRUE
    `the only step taken is requiring manual entry of age or date of birth`               IS FALSE
    `the only step taken is requiring an approved evidence of age document`               IS FALSE
    `the only step taken is using a digital identity service`                             IS FALSE
    `the only steps taken are an evidence of age document and a digital identity service` IS TRUE
    `the steps taken are otherwise reasonable`                                            IS TRUE
    `collects personal information of a class that regulations under section 63 forbid`   IS FALSE

-- A change to the terms of use, assessed and filed in time.
`a compliant terms change` MEANS `change related assessment` WITH
    name                                                                                 IS "terms of use rewrite"
    `the proposed change is a significant change to design, features or functionality`    IS FALSE
    `the proposed change is a significant change to the terms of use`                     IS TRUE
    `an assessment of the section 14(2) matters was undertaken before the change was made` IS TRUE
    `is in writing`                                                                      IS TRUE
    `describes the anticipated levels of risk and the reasons for them`                   IS TRUE
    `describes current measures, their expected efficacy and any additional measures`     IS TRUE
    `describes the method used to assess the section 14(2) matters for the change`        IS TRUE
    `a copy was provided to the regulator as soon as practicable after the assessment`    IS TRUE
    `a copy was provided to the regulator before the change was made`                     IS TRUE

-- The same change, assessed but filed only after the change went live.
`a late-filed terms change` MEANS `change related assessment` WITH
    name                                                                                 IS "terms of use rewrite, filed after launch"
    `the proposed change is a significant change to design, features or functionality`    IS FALSE
    `the proposed change is a significant change to the terms of use`                     IS TRUE
    `an assessment of the section 14(2) matters was undertaken before the change was made` IS TRUE
    `is in writing`                                                                      IS TRUE
    `describes the anticipated levels of risk and the reasons for them`                   IS TRUE
    `describes current measures, their expected efficacy and any additional measures`     IS TRUE
    `describes the method used to assess the section 14(2) matters for the change`        IS TRUE
    `a copy was provided to the regulator as soon as practicable after the assessment`    IS TRUE
    `a copy was provided to the regulator before the change was made`                     IS FALSE

-- A designation of someone with no real role in the assessments.
`a nominal designation` MEANS `responsible individual designation` WITH
    name                                                                                 IS "a junior compliance analyst"
    `an individual has been designated by notice to the regulator`                        IS TRUE
    `the individual has a significant role in ensuring or overseeing the risk assessments` IS FALSE
    `the notice specifies the designated individual's contact details`                    IS TRUE

§§ `Machine-evaluated cases`

#EVAL `the operator satisfies the duty in section 11(1)` `compliant age assurance`
#ASSERT `the operator satisfies the duty in section 11(1)` `compliant age assurance` EQUALS TRUE

-- cl 11(3)(c): an operator that does both formal identity checks and nothing
-- else does not satisfy the duty, however reasonable those checks are.
#EVAL `the operator satisfies the duty in section 11(1)` `identity documents only`
#ASSERT `the steps taken cannot satisfy the duty` `identity documents only` EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `the operator satisfies the duty in section 11(1)` `identity documents only` EQUALS FALSE

#ASSERT `the operator complies with section 17` `a compliant terms change` EQUALS TRUE

-- cl 17(3)(b): the copy must reach the regulator before the change is made.
#EVAL `the operator complies with section 17` `a late-filed terms change`
#ASSERT `the operator complies with section 17` `a late-filed terms change` EQUALS FALSE

-- cl 18(2): designation of someone without a significant role is not a valid
-- designation, so the operator has not complied with cl 18 at all.
#ASSERT `the operator has validly designated a responsible individual` `a nominal designation` EQUALS FALSE
